[1mScope.[22m The project is a single function: [38;5;10munsigned hdr_bitrate(const uint8_t *h)[0m, an MPEG audio-frame bitrate table lookup. [38;5;10mtranslation/Cargo.toml[0m has no [38;5;10m[features][0m section and [38;5;10mc_src/CMakeLists.txt[0m has no build options, so there is exactly one valid configuration — the default/empty feature set. No [38;5;10m#[cfg(feature = ...)][0m gating was needed.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1mSymbol parity.[22m The C [38;5;10m.so[0m exports one non-toolchain symbol, [38;5;10mhdr_bitrate[0m; the Rust [38;5;10mcdylib[0m exports it too. No macro-generated symbols exist in the C. Verified by [38;5;10mnm -D[0m and by an automated test ([38;5;10mtests/symbol_parity.rs[0m).[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1mDifferential results.[22m All 65536 distinct inputs (only [38;5;10mh[1][0m and [38;5;10mh[2][0m are read) produce byte-identical results between the two [38;5;10m.so[0m files, against the CMake build and against [38;5;10mcc[0m at [38;5;10m-O0/-O1/-O2/-O3/-Os[0m. 14 tests pass in both debug and release.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1mThe interesting part[22m is the two out-of-bounds indexings the C performs, which the translation deliberately preserves:[0m[0m
[0m[0m
- [38;5;10m((h[1] >> 1) & 3) - 1[0m is [38;5;10m-1[0m for the reserved layer, indexing a row [3mbefore[23m the selected plane.[0m[0m
- [38;5;10mh[2] >> 4[0m reaches 15, but the innermost dimension is 15 wide.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
Flat offsets into the 90-byte table span [38;5;10m-15..=90[0m. Most are still inside the flat array (so the Rust flat table reproduces them exactly); genuinely out-of-bounds are offsets [38;5;10m-15..=-1[0m and [38;5;10m90[0m, covering 8192 of the 65536 inputs. The existing Rust code pads the table with 15 zero bytes in front and 1 behind. I confirmed with [38;5;10mreadelf[0m/[38;5;10mod[0m that this is what the C actually reads: the table sits at the very start of [38;5;10m.rodata[0m ([38;5;10m0x2000[0m, size exactly [38;5;10m0x5a[0m), and the surrounding bytes are section alignment padding — zeros both before and after — at every optimization level. So the padding reproduces the C rather than merely being memory-safe.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1mTwo things I had to add[22m to make [38;5;10mcargo test[0m self-sufficient:[0m[0m
[0m[0m
- [38;5;10mlibloading = "0.8"[0m in [38;5;10m[dev-dependencies][0m.[0m[0m
- Cargo does not build a [38;5;10mcdylib[0m-only library target for integration tests (it only needs the crate's [38;5;10mrmeta[0m), so [38;5;10mtarget/debug/libhdr_bitrate_lib.so[0m never appears. [38;5;10mtests/common/mod.rs[0m builds it on demand via a nested [38;5;10mcargo build --lib[0m into a separate [38;5;10mtarget/ffi-cdylib[0m directory, which avoids blocking on the build-directory lock the outer [38;5;10mcargo test[0m holds. Verified from a clean target.[0m[0m
